      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5c8a4c682bb5373bfeb85af2",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree with Gacha, the current report system could use some improvements first before this becomes a thing but I do think down the line this is a function needed in VRC as there is A LOT of toxicity and rule-breaking things (both avatars and worlds). Foxx points out a few good things as well but it can very easily be avoided on the staff side of things by having utilizing a filter that puts specific reports to a spam type folder to ignore and the more important things to a priority inbox. May not fully avoid all of it but it will improve sorting out what's important as a report and what isn't. \nA simple part to the filter could simply be including a screenshot in the report of exactly what the issue is.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
